From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:40:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mailbox: apple: add the secure RTBuddy port

A coprocessor can have a second mailbox for its secure side, the ADT's
iop,secure-rtbuddy-proxy. It has the registers of the AOP setup port,
and its interrupts aren't described yet, so its consumer polls it. Add
its compatible, and require interrupts for every mailbox but this one.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
---
 .../bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml       | 20 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
index 04fbc40f01..90ee540ace 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
@@ -66,6 +66,14 @@ properties:
           AOP setup-port mailbox with a separate register layout.
         const: apple,t8140-aop-setup-mailbox
 
+      - description:
+          A coprocessor's secure RTBuddy port, the ADT's
+          iop,secure-rtbuddy-proxy. It is polled, with no interrupts described.
+        items:
+          - enum:
+              - apple,t8140-secure-rtbuddy-proxy
+          - const: apple,secure-rtbuddy-proxy
+
       - description:
           An older ASC mailbox interface found on T2 and A11 that is also
           used for the NVMe coprocessor and the system management
@@ -124,6 +132,16 @@ properties:
     maxItems: 2
 
 allOf:
+  - if:
+      not:
+        properties:
+          compatible:
+            contains:
+              const: apple,secure-rtbuddy-proxy
+    then:
+      required:
+        - interrupts
+        - interrupt-names
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
@@ -186,8 +204,6 @@ allOf:
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
-  - interrupts
-  - interrupt-names
   - "#mbox-cells"
 
 additionalProperties: false
